{"timestamp": 1779428809.8847265, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 18, "data": {"caller": "player_1", "reason": "Bob reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "security", "victim_name": "Diana"}, {"room": "oxygen", "victim_name": "Alice"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779428809.8860233, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 18, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779428817.2006068, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I found Diana dead in security. My route this round was from lower engine through storage, medbay, cafeteria, weapons, and finally into security where I stumbled on the body. I haven't run into a single other person this entire round, so I don't have any leads on who might have done this. Did anyone see someone heading away from the right side of the map recently? Also, sounds like Alice might be dead too?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779428829.4297602, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I went from medbay to upper engine, then down to lower engine, and ended up in storage. At tick 9, I saw Alice in upper engine \u2014 she had just come in from medbay. Since she's dead now, she might have been killed somewhere on the left side of the map shortly after I saw her, unless she moved elsewhere. \n\nBob, I didn't see you in lower engine or storage, but we might have just missed each other while I was in upper engine or moving between rooms. I haven't seen Eve or Frank at all this round. \n\nEve, Frank \u2014 where were you guys? One of you must have been near security for Diana, and potentially near upper engine for Alice. Let's get all the routes out there before we make any decisions. Since there are 4 of us left, we have to be careful with our votes today."}}
{"timestamp": 1779428869.6281614, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I started on the left side \u2014 oxygen/upper engine \u2014 then went across through cafeteria and weapons. I did briefly go into security and Diana was alive when I saw her there, so Bob finding her there later makes me a little nervous about that report timing. After that I went electrical, saw Eve there, then medbay and back toward upper engine. Eve was with me near the end in upper engine.\n\nI never saw Alice this round, so Charlie being the last one placing her in upper engine is important. Right now it sounds like Diana died on right side and Alice likely died left side, so I don\u2019t think we should tunnel one person without hearing Eve. But Bob self-reporting security and Charlie being near Alice\u2019s last known location are both worth looking at."}}
{"timestamp": 1779428984.4197412, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I can 100% clear Frank, which means the Duck is definitively either Bob or Charlie. \n\nHere is my exact timeline and why Frank is mathematically innocent:\nI went from Weapons -> Security -> Electrical -> Medbay -> Upper Engine. \nI saw Diana alive in Security at ticks 6, 7, and 8 (she had just entered from Electrical at T6). \nAt tick 12, I was in Electrical and I saw Frank walk in from Security. After that, Frank and I basically moved together through Medbay and ended the round together in Upper Engine.\n\nSince there are two dead bodies, the single Duck had to kill both Alice and Diana. Charlie claims Alice was alive in Upper Engine at tick 9. For Frank to have killed Alice at T9 in Upper Engine, he would have had to travel across the entire map to Security/Electrical by T12. That's a minimum 6-tick journey, meaning he couldn't possibly be there until T15. Even if Charlie is lying about seeing Alice, that just means Charlie is the Duck. Either way, Frank is entirely cleared.\n\nThat leaves Bob and Charlie. Interestingly, Charlie claims to have gone Lower Engine -> Storage, and Bob claims to have gone Lower Engine -> Storage -> Medbay, yet neither of you saw each other. One of you is lying, and one of you is the Duck. \n\nHowever, since there are exactly 4 of us left, this is LYLO (Losing Your Life Opportunity). If we guess wrong on a 50/50 between Bob and Charlie, it becomes 2 Geese vs 1 Duck, and we instantly lose when the Duck gets their next kill. If we skip, we go into the next round with 4 people, the Duck kills one of the suspects or clears, and we have a much safer 3-person final vote.\n\nFrank, you and I are completely cleared to each other. Stick to me like glue this next round. If anyone else approaches us, we run. I am voting to SKIP, and I strongly advise everyone else to do the same so we don't throw the game on a coin flip.\n\nskip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779429000.3330739, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "skip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779429011.9548287, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "skip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779429058.8295643, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 18, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I\u2019m with Eve here. From my perspective, Eve and I were together late enough that I\u2019m not voting her, and she\u2019s right that this looks like Bob vs Charlie.\n\nBob reports Diana in security, and Charlie is the one who placed Alice near upper engine shortly before she died. Their routes also overlap weirdly through lower engine/storage without seeing each other, so one of those stories is probably off.\n\nThat said, with 4 alive I don\u2019t want to coin-flip and hand the game over if we\u2019re wrong. I\u2019m also voting skip. Next round, Eve and I stick together, and Bob/Charlie need to stay separated or we\u2019ll know exactly what\u2019s happening."}}
