{"timestamp": 1779429382.650416, "event_type": "free_roam_chat", "tick": 32, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "name": "Charlie", "room": "cafeteria", "message": "Hey Bob, let's stick together. Only 3 of us left.", "tick": 32}}
{"timestamp": 1779429390.297668, "event_type": "meeting_called", "tick": 32, "data": {"caller": "player_1", "reason": "Bob called an emergency meeting", "bodies": [{"room": "storage", "victim_name": "Eve"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779429390.298722, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 32, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779429404.2482665, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 32, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I called this emergency meeting because we are at final 3 and I know Eve is dead in storage. Frank, I saw you in navigation with Eve around tick 24, and then you headed towards storage at tick 25. Charlie just walked into the cafeteria from electrical at tick 32. Based on this, Frank had the perfect opportunity to kill Eve in storage. Charlie, please vote Frank with me, it has to be him."}}
{"timestamp": 1779429416.3115149, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 32, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Bob, you just slipped up massively. You called an emergency meeting from the button in the cafeteria, but you claim you *know* Eve is dead down in storage. If you had actually found her body in storage, you would have just reported it there. The only way you could possibly know she's dead in storage while standing in the cafeteria is if you killed her yourself! \n\nOn top of that, I saw you walk into the cafeteria from weapons, nowhere near storage. You're trying to frame Frank because we're at final three, but your story makes no sense. Frank, vote Bob with me, he just gave himself away!"}}
{"timestamp": 1779429440.1724706, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 32, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Bob, that doesn\u2019t add up. I was in navigation with you and Eve, yes, but I left through storage toward lower engine and never saw or reported a body. I had no idea Eve was dead until you said it.\n\nCharlie\u2019s point is the big one: you called the button from cafeteria but somehow \u201cknow\u201d Eve is dead in storage. If you found the body, you\u2019d report it. If you didn\u2019t find it, how do you know exactly where she died?\n\nAlso you were already the one reporting earlier, and now at final 3 you\u2019re trying to hard-frame me with information you shouldn\u2019t have. Charlie, I\u2019m with you \u2014 this is Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1779429449.3837626, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 32, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Frank"}}
{"timestamp": 1779429457.354256, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 32, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Bob"}}
{"timestamp": 1779429468.4304233, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 32, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Bob, your route and your info still don\u2019t line up.\n\nI\u2019ll be clear with my path: I went medbay \u2192 storage \u2192 navigation, where I saw you and Eve around tick 24/25. Then I left back through storage and ended up lower engine. Eve also came into storage after that, but I never saw a body there and I never reported anything.\n\nThe problem is you\u2019re saying you \u201cknow\u201d Eve is dead in storage while calling button from cafeteria. That\u2019s not normal crewmate info. If you actually saw her body, you report it. If you didn\u2019t see it, you shouldn\u2019t know the exact location.\n\nCharlie\u2019s account makes more sense to me: you came from weapons into cafeteria, hit the button, and immediately tried to pin it on me with info you shouldn\u2019t have. At final three, that looks like the duck trying to force a misvote.\n\nI\u2019m voting Bob."}}
